@*
    How a shelf is measured. Posted as `soldByLength`, which the controller
    takes alongside the category.

    Two options and no "follow the name", unlike the product form: a category
    IS the thing a name would be read off, so leaving it implicit here would
    mean the screen could not show an answer at all. Editing an existing
    category preselects whatever it is measured by today, so saving without
    touching this changes nothing.
*@
@{
    var soldByLength = ViewData["SoldByLength"] as bool? ?? false;
}

<div class="mb-3">
    <label class="form-label">Measured by</label>
    <div class="measure-choice">
        <label class="measure-option">
            <span class="measure-option-head">
                <input class="form-check-input mt-0" type="radio" name="soldByLength"
                       value="false" checked="@(!soldByLength)" />
                Counted in pieces
            </span>
            <span class="measure-option-help">
                Stock is whole units. One line on a job takes one piece off the shelf.
            </span>
        </label>

        <label class="measure-option">
            <span class="measure-option-head">
                <input class="form-check-input mt-0" type="radio" name="soldByLength"
                       value="true" checked="@soldByLength" />
                Measured by length
            </span>
            <span class="measure-option-help">
                Roll goods. Stock is kept in centimetres, deliveries and counts
                can be entered in cm, in or m, and a tint job deducts the cut
                size for each panel.
            </span>
        </label>
    </div>
</div>
